WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:05.270
An angular unconformity begins with layers deposited approximately horizontally.

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:08.050
Later deformation tilts or folds them.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:12.630
Erosion then cuts across the tilted beds, and younger sediment buries

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:16.470
the surface. Watch the old layers remain truncated beneath the new

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:20.530
cover. The contact records several events and missing time, rather than

00:00:20.530 --> 00:00:22.050
one unusually thick bed.

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:26.610
A nonconformity forms when deep crystalline rock, such as granite, reaches

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:28.450
the surface through uplift and erosion.

00:00:28.750 --> 00:00:30.750
Weathering can alter its exposed top.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.830
Younger sediment then covers the eroded granite and eventually becomes sedimentary

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:39.810
rock. The critical relationship is sedimentary cover above eroded nonlayered crystalline

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:40.110
basement.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:46.090
A disconformity separates sedimentary packages whose beds remain parallel.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:51.010
Deposition stops, erosion or nondeposition removes part of the record, and

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:55.530
sedimentation resumes. Because the packages can look similar, the gap may

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:59.290
be difficult to recognize. Fossil age ranges can reveal missing time

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:01.350
even when the contact is visually subtle.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:05.830
The Grand Canyon and Ouray photographs show older steep or tilted

00:01:05.830 --> 00:01:09.850
rock beneath younger cover. Follow the actual boundary and compare bedding

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:14.430
on both sides. Some examples involve metamorphic layering, so state the

00:01:14.430 --> 00:01:17.190
visible relationships rather than relying on one color.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:21.090
The textbook names and photographs provide the context for classification.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:25.660
Every unconformity is younger than the rock it truncates and older

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:26.940
than the deposits above it.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.300
Ages on those rocks bracket missing time;

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:32.380
they do not recover every event removed by erosion.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:35.920
Name the type, explain the required sequence, and state what the

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:38.520
preserved evidence cannot tell you about the missing interval.
